      "problem": "Which of the following represents the level curves of $f(x,y)=y-x?$",
      "worked_solution": "The level curves for the function $f(x,y)$ are given by the equations \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=c.\n$$\n\nNotice that the range of $f(x,y)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ So, we will consider level curves for any value of $c.$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =c \\\\ y-x & =c \\\\ y & =x+c.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation above gives us a family of lines with slope of $1.$ Therefore, the correct graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14135461/assets/91fde8bc9eb57c1974e622a6673a030c9889c77d6788b620ffe70d7d6a8409c5.png)",
